---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="MastersVault has no accounts and keeps your data in your browser.">
  <div class="container page prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is a static website hosted on GitHub Pages. It has no accounts, no sign-in, no advertising and no
      cookies. It counts page views with a privacy-focused service, described under "Page views" below.
    </p>

    <h2>What's stored, and where</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your test attempts and progress</strong> are saved in your browser's local storage on this device.
        They are never sent to us or anyone else.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Your colour-theme choice</strong> is saved the same way.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Copies of pages and tests you have opened</strong> are kept on this device so that the site still
        works without an internet connection. They contain only the site's own content, nothing about you.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Clearing your browser's site data deletes all of this. On the dashboard you can export it to a file, import
      it on another device, or delete it all at once.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      Like any web host, GitHub may log basic request information such as IP addresses when pages are served. See
      GitHub's privacy statement for details. {SITE.name} has no access to those logs.
    </p>

    <h2>Page views</h2>
    <p>
      The site counts page views with <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/">GoatCounter</a>, an open-source
      analytics service. The footer's visitor count comes from it. GoatCounter stores nothing in your browser (no
      cookies and no local storage) and doesn't keep your IP address.
    </p>
    <p>
      For each page view it records the page's address, the site that linked to it, your browser, operating system
      and language, your screen width, and your approximate location, which it works out from your IP address. These
      are kept as totals, not as a record of what any one visitor did. To avoid counting the same visit twice, it
      holds your IP address and browser details in memory for up to eight hours. Nothing about your answers, scores
      or progress is sent. See <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/help/privacy">GoatCounter's privacy policy</a> for
      details.
    </p>
    <p>An ad blocker that blocks the counter doesn't affect how the site works.</p>

    <h2>Fonts and third parties</h2>
    <p>
      The page-view counter is the only thing loaded from another site. The fonts, scripts and everything else are
      served from the same origin, and there are no third-party embeds.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
